Format = Name, Type, Ra, Dec, I, SpectralIndex, LogarithmicSI, ReferenceFrequency, MajorAxis, MinorAxis, Orientation
# References:
# Flux model use wsclean format
# Fluxes and positions from B.Hugo model. Derived from transfer calibration described in Modelling of PKS B1934-638 (J193925.0-634245) as UHF and L-Band calibrator for MeerKAT
# Warning: this model is artificially truncated to the top 90 smeared responses
# Flux scale (2026-11): rescaled to the SARAO knowledge-base polynomial (Partridge et al. 2016 coefficients,
#   Flux and bandpass calibration page), log10(S/Jy) = -0.9790 + 3.3662 L - 1.1216 L^2 + 0.0861 L^3, L = log10(nu/MHz):
#   every component multiplied by SARAO/(model flux within 2 arcmin) and refitted with two more polynomial terms,
#   so the component structure and field sources are kept. The original katsdpcal model is in git history.
#   The katsdpcal UHF model was 10% below SARAO at 850-1000 MHz and 10% above at 544 MHz. Below 900 MHz the
#   SARAO polynomial is extrapolated; MRC/PKSCAT90 (408 MHz) and RACS-low (888 MHz) are within 3% of it,
#   and a fit through GLEAM-X, MRC, SUMSS, RACS-low, PKSCAT90 and PMN is within 1% of it over 544-1088 MHz.
